<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Foligno</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Foligno is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umbria">Umbria</a>, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, in the plain below <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assisi">Assisi</a> on the old Via Flaminia. A medieval commune and rival of Perugia, it was ruled by the Trinci family from 1305 until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> took it in 1439. The first printed edition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/divine-comedy">Divine Comedy</a> was produced there in 1472.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/foligno.jpg" alt="Foligno" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Skvaril · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Foligno_6.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
